In article <1993May19.012529.6546@beaver.cs.washington.edu>, duyphan@cs.washington.edu (Haldan Orlav) writes:
>>>3) It's possible for identical objects (food rations, potions) to take up
>>>two inventory slots. Yes, I had identified their cursed/non-cursed status.
>>
>>	Yes the reason for this is that you probably picked up another
>>food ration and then identified it.  Nethack does not have any merging
>>capabilityies when you are carrying items. solution, workaround, drop
>>all your food then pick it back up and it'll be in one slot.
>>
>This has also happened to me, twice.  I identified two uncursed scrolls of
>scared monster.  Then I put them both in my bag of holding and take them
>out again.  They refused to merge.  However, when I dropped them, they merged.
>Of course, you know what happens to scrolls of scare monster when you drop
>them.  Maybe scrolls of scare monster don't like bags of holding ? 
>

If you have two identical things in different inventory slots, and you want
to merge them, instead of just dropping them and picking them up again you
can use the #adjust command.  It takes no turns, and it doesn't affect the
scare monster scrolls.
